From 8f5c2a6c2ca1a4462f0fb74604e9fe0ecb2a1e6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:29:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] hsdir: Add off-by-default unknown-prev-hop and
 circuit-reuse defenses

Allow HSDirs to refuse anonymous onion service directory requests
whose previous hop is not a known relay (HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop /
hsdir_refuse_unknown_prev_hop, with a 503 response) and to close
circuits that make more than one onion service directory request
(HSDirOneRequestPerCircuit / hsdir_one_request_per_circ, with reason
RESOURCELIMIT). Both options default to auto (count-only unless enabled
by torrc or consensus).
