diff --git a/changes/ticket41339_hsdir_circ_reuse b/changes/ticket41339_hsdir_circ_reuse
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..917babd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changes/ticket41339_hsdir_circ_reuse
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+  o Minor features (DoS-resistance, onion service directory):
+    - HSDirs now count every circuit that makes more than one onion service
+      descriptor fetch or upload, and can close it (with reason
+      RESOURCELIMIT). Tor and Arti make each such request on its own circuit,
+      so this only affects clients that reuse a circuit to multiply their
+      requests. The reuse is counted in the DoS heartbeat ("circuits with
+      repeated HSDir requests") and in the
+      tor_relay_dos_total{type="hsdir_circ_reused"},
+      {type="hsdir_req_reused"}, and {type="hsdir_request_total"} MetricsPort
+      metrics. Closing is off by default (counting only): it is controlled by
+      the new HSDirOneRequestPerCircuit torrc option, which overrides the new
+      "hsdir_one_request_per_circ" consensus parameter, which in turn defaults
+      to off so that a relay with no opinion only observes. Part of ticket
+      41339.
diff --git a/changes/ticket41339_hsdir_known_relay b/changes/ticket41339_hsdir_known_relay
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a4e87e0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changes/ticket41339_hsdir_known_relay
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+  o Minor features (onion service directory, DoS):
+    - HSDirs can now refuse onion service descriptor fetches and uploads whose
+      previous hop is not a known relay (in the consensus or with a
+      descriptor), and count the rest. Anyone can authenticate with a
+      self-generated relay key, so such requests could be single hop, which
+      HSDirs have refused from clients since 0.4.2.1-alpha. This rejects
+      arbitrary unknown prev-hop identities; it does not rate limit, since an
+      attacker can add one hop through any consensus relay. Refusing is off by
+      default (counting only): it is the new HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop torrc
+      option and "hsdir_refuse_unknown_prev_hop" consensus parameter, both
+      independent of RefuseUnknownExits. The only false positives are in the
+      roughly 1e-6 per-request window when a relay has not yet seen the
+      previous hop in a fresh consensus. Part of ticket 41339.
diff --git a/doc/man/tor.1.txt b/doc/man/tor.1.txt
index a865ebd..5ba5549 100644
--- a/doc/man/tor.1.txt
+++ b/doc/man/tor.1.txt
@@ -3148,6 +3148,37 @@ The following options are useful only for a exit relay.
     not defined or set to 0, it is controlled by a consensus parameter. If not
     defined in the consensus, the value is 300. (Default: 0)
 
+The following options are useful only for an onion service directory (HSDir).
+
+[[HSDirOneRequestPerCircuit]] **HSDirOneRequestPerCircuit** **0**|**1**|**auto**::
+
+    Tor and Arti make each onion service descriptor fetch and upload on its
+    own circuit, so a circuit that carries more than one is not a stock
+    client. If set to 1, an HSDir closes such a circuit (with reason
+    RESOURCELIMIT) on the second request; if 0, it only counts them. "auto"
+    means use the hsdir_one_request_per_circ consensus parameter, and only
+    count if the consensus is silent. This option thus overrides the
+    consensus, which overrides the default of counting only. The reuse is
+    counted (in the heartbeat and as
+    tor_relay_dos_total{type="hsdir_circ_reused"},
+    {type="hsdir_req_reused"}, and {type="hsdir_request_total"}) in every
+    case, so an operator or authority can measure the effect before enabling
+    enforcement. (Default: auto)
+
+[[HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop]] **HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop** **0**|**1**|**auto**::
+
+    Since 0.4.2.1-alpha an HSDir refuses onion service descriptor fetches and
+    uploads from client channels, so they can't be made over one-hop circuits.
+    But a peer can authenticate with any self-generated relay identity, which
+    is not a client channel. If set to 1, an HSDir refuses (with a 503) such a
+    request whose previous hop is not a relay in its consensus or for which it
+    has a descriptor; if 0, it only counts them. "auto" means use the
+    hsdir_refuse_unknown_prev_hop consensus parameter, and only count if the
+    consensus is silent. This option, and that parameter, are independent of
+    RefuseUnknownExits, so turning this off does not weaken exit protection.
+    The count appears in the heartbeat and as
+    tor_relay_dos_total{type="hsdir_unknown_prev_hop"}. (Default: auto)
+
 
 For onion services, mitigations are a work in progress and multiple options
 are currently available.
